   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 81 of the laws of 1995, amending the public health law\nand other laws relating to medical reimbursement and welfare reform, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness of certain provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7479",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7479-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §246, Chap 81 of 1995",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7479\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 81 of the laws of 1995, amending the public\nhealth law and other laws relating to medical reimbursement and welfare\nreform, in relation to extending the effectiveness of certain provisions\nthereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend various provisions of the public health law related to Limited\nLicensed Home Care Services Agencies and ensure these critical health\ncare facilities can continue operating in New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Extends, subdivision 12 of section 246 of chapter 81 of the\nlaws of 1995, which relates to limited home care services agencies,\nuntil June 30, 2025.\n\nSection 2: Effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is necessary to ensure the continuation of specific laws of\ncritical importance to the Department of Health relating to limited\nlicensed home care services agencies in order to avoid the expiration of\nthose laws. Limited Licensed Home Care Services Agencies provide\npersonal care services, nursing supervision, intramuscular injections,\nand other administrative tasks laid out in federal regulations and\nrequire this bill to continue operation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
